ain, gate and source connections. The body connection on the M6 slot looks spurious, so I'd drop it.\n\nNow I'm deciding on the net names for the pins, since every pin currently sits on the merged net1. I'll give each node its own name, such as latch, nA, and nB, and reassign all of the pins to them.\n\nNow I'm assigning each pin on M1 through M5 to its new net name, starting with the gate on M1 that moves off net2 onto the latch node.\n\nNow I'm writing out the remaining pin assignments for M6 through M13, sending each drain, gate and source to its new net and dropping the spurious body connection on M6.\n\n",
